<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple Kick Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Watch multiple Kick streams and chats at once. Learn how to add channels, build a flexible layout, and troubleshoot Kick embeds in Stream Mix."
  heading="Watch multiple Kick streams at once"
  platform="kick"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix puts multiple Kick channels and chats in one draggable browser
    workspace, with each panel showing video, chat, or both.
  </p>

  <h2>How to add multiple Kick streams</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Paste a channel URL such as <code>https://kick.com/xqc</code> into the Stream
      Mix header.
    </li>
    <li>
      Kick is selected automatically. Choose Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat.
    </li>
    <li>Select <strong>Add</strong> and repeat for the remaining channels.</li>
    <li>Drag and resize the resulting windows to arrange your layout.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    You can also select Kick manually and enter only the channel name. Channel
    URLs and names are supported; clips and VOD pages are not.
  </p>

  <h2>Kick embed behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix uses Kick’s official player and pop-out chat—it does not restream
    broadcasts. Kick remains responsible for playback controls, chat, account
    access, and content availability.
  </p>

  <p>
    Chat and account features can depend on Kick authentication, cookies, and
    content-blocking extensions. Kick documents its player in the{" "}
    <a
      href="https://help.kick.com/en/articles/8010826-how-to-embed-your-kick-livestream"
      rel="external">official embedding guide</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Kick troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>URL rejected:</strong> use the main channel URL or channel name, not
      a category, search, dashboard, clip, or VOD page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Channel appears offline:</strong> the window remains saved and can
      stay in your layout for the creator’s next broadcast.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Chat or account controls fail:</strong> check the channel directly
      on Kick, then test without strict tracking protection or content blockers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Several streams stutter:</strong> lower secondary stream quality, mute
      unused audio, use Chat-only panels, or minimize some streams.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related guides</h2>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams">setup guide</a>, or add{
      " "
    }
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-twitch-streams">Twitch</a> and{" "}
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-youtube-streams">YouTube</a> streams to the same
    workspace. The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> covers saved layouts, privacy, and common
    embed behavior.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the Kick multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
